dnight after all data for March 1 becomes available. This is why a DAG is a=
lways executed at the end of the data interval, and the logical date of a D=
AG run (start of the data interval) represents the date </span></span><span=
><em><strong><span>for</span></strong></em></span><span><span> which the DA=
G run is executed, not when the DAG is actually executed. So the first DAG =
